course: dictionary
lesson: 4524
title: Headquarters: the main base
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A headquarters is the main office, the place where a company, army, police force or organisation is run from. In «The biggest is the United Nations... its headquarters is in New York», the clue is the word "its": the headquarters belongs to the organisation and is where its work is directed. Swap in "main office" to check: "its main office is in New York" still makes sense.
explain: Headquarters ends in s, so it can look plural, but it is often used as one word for one place, as in «police headquarters» or «company headquarters». Its short form is HQ.
explain: In games and stories, HQ means the base, the place a team goes back to, as in «back to HQ». The idea is the same as in the news: it is the central place where everything is organised.
fact: Headquarters means the main office or base from which an organisation is run.
fact: Headquarters can be singular or plural, and HQ is the short form.
fact: «The United Nations» was founded in 1945 after the Second World War, and its headquarters is in New York.
fact: The African Union links all 55 African countries, and its headquarters is in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia.
fact: In games and stories, «back to HQ» means back to the base.
exercise: «The United Nations has its headquarters in New York.» Where is its main office? | London | Addis Ababa | *New York | Paris
exercise: In a game, what does «back to HQ» mean? | *Go back to the base | Go home for tea | Go to the shop | Go to sleep
exercise: What does headquarters mean? | A kitchen where food is made | *The main office where an organisation is run | A type of cloud | A sports field
test: «The African Union links 55 countries, and its headquarters is in Addis Ababa.» What is a headquarters? | Any small room | *The main office or base | A river crossing | A holiday home
test: Which phrase uses headquarters in the same way as «company headquarters»? | a sunny beach | *police headquarters | a hot drink | a school lunch
exam: «Its headquarters is in New York.» In this sentence, headquarters means what? | A kind of game | A type of weather | A place to sleep | *The main office from which the organisation is run
